const geo = useMemo(() => {
  const g = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
  g.setAttribute("position", new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(MAX_SPARKS*3), 3));
  g.setAttribute("aColor", new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(MAX_SPARKS*3), 3));
  g.setAttribute("aSize", new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(MAX_SPARKS), 1));
  g.setAttribute("aAlpha", new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(MAX_SPARKS), 1));
  g.setDrawRange(0,0);
  return g;
}, []);
```

Shader material:
```ts
const mat = useMemo(() => new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
  uniforms: { uScale: { value: 300 } },
  vertexShader: `...`,
  fragmentShader: `...`,
  transparent: true,
  depthWrite: false,
  blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,
}), []);
```

vertex:
```glsl
attribute vec3 aColor;
attribute float aSize;
attribute float aAlpha;
uniform float uScale;
varying vec3 vC;
varying float vA;
void main(){
  vC = aColor; vA = aAlpha;
  vec4 mv = modelViewMatrix * vec4(position, 1.0);
  gl_PointSize = aSize * uScale / max(0.001, -mv.z);
  gl_Position = projectionMatrix * mv;
}
```

fragment:
```glsl
varying vec3 vC; varying float vA;
void main(){
  vec2 uv = gl_PointCoord - 0.5;
  float d = length(uv);
  if (d > 0.5) discard;
  float a = smoothstep(0.5, 0.0, d);
  a = pow(a, 1.6);
  gl_FragColor = vec4(vC * (0.6 + a * 1.6), a * vA);
}
```

Then useFrame: update fx, fill buffers.

For miles: separate Points with same material but bigger uScale.

Actually I can render motes and sparks in the same Points if I write both into the same buffers — motes are just particles with life. But motes need their positions from bezier each frame. I could convert motes to "particle" entries at write time: for each mote, compute position and write with size 1.6, alpha 1. And sparks after. Total capacity = MAX_MOTES + MAX_SPARKS.

That's simpler: one draw call.

So buffer capacity = MAX_SPARKS + MAX_MOTES.

Write:
- for each mote: pos, color, size 1.5, alpha 1
- for each spark: pos, color, size s.size, alpha = min(1, life/max * 2)

