    if (buf[i] === 0x28 && buf[i+1] === 0xb5 && buf[i+2] === 0x2f && buf[i+3] === 0xfd) offs.push(i);
  }
  return offs;
}

export function decodeBuffer(buf) {
  // 返回 { text, consumed } —— consumed 是已完整解出的字节数
}
```

For incremental tailing, I need to know how many bytes were fully consumed (last complete frame end). Since frames are concatenated, the last magic offset marks the start of the last frame — which may be incomplete. So: decode all frames except possibly the last; consumed = offset of last magic (if decoding the last frame failed) else buf.length.

